   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Tener que and hay que",
     "texto": [
      "**Tener que** + infinitive says who has to do it:\n\n- **tengo que** estudiar (I)\n- **tienes que** estudiar (you)\n- **tiene que** estudiar (he, she)\n\n**Hay que** + infinitive expresses a general obligation and never changes: **hay que** llegar a las nueve.\n\nUse **porque** to give a reason: estudio **porque** mañana hay un examen. **¿Por qué?** (two words, with an accent) asks «why?»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Who has to do it?",
     "texto": [
      "**Tener que** changes with the person (**tengo que**, **tiene que**). **Hay que** never changes. An infinitive always follows both."
     ],
     "ejemplos": [
